# Project Rules: ICD11

This project is an Astro-based website.

## Working rules

- Preserve the existing Astro project structure.
- Do not change routes unless explicitly requested.
- Do not rename files or folders unless explicitly requested.
- Do not introduce new libraries without asking first.
- Prefer the smallest safe change.
- Do not make large refactors unless explicitly requested.
- Before editing, inspect the relevant files and understand the existing implementation.

## Design and UX rules

- Preserve the existing visual identity of the website.
- Improve readability, spacing, visual hierarchy, responsiveness, and accessibility.
- Keep the design professional, polished, and consistent.
- Do not redesign the whole site unless explicitly asked.
- Always consider mobile responsiveness.

## Code quality

- Follow the existing formatting and project conventions.
- Keep code clean, readable, and maintainable.
- Avoid unnecessary JavaScript.
- Prefer simple Astro/static solutions where possible.
- After making changes, explain what changed, which files changed, and how to test locally.

## Deployment

- Keep the project compatible with its current deployment setup.
- Do not change deployment-related files unless explicitly requested.